## Why This Is Asked

Interview context explanation.

## Key Concepts

- Edge computing
- Data minimization
- Cache coherence
- Privacy budgets

## Code Example

```javascript
function edgeScore(userMasked, locale, region) {
  const seed = userMasked + locale + region;
  let h = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < seed.length; i++) {
    h = (h * 31 + seed.charCodeAt(i)) | 0;
  }
  return Math.abs(h) % 100;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test determinism of the edge heuristic across restarts?
- How would you handle policy changes that affect downstream scores?

## Why This Is Asked
Gauges how well a candidate designs feature-level gating in a per-user scoring API, a practical knob for privacy, performance, and experimentation.

## Key Concepts
- Feature gating: filter features at the API boundary.
- Deterministic scoring: gating should not introduce nondeterminism.
- Validation & observability: log gating decisions for audits.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: apply feature gating before scoring
function computeScoreWithGating(allFeatures, allowedFeatures){
  const mask = new Set(allowedFeatures || allFeatures.map(f => f.name));
  const included = allFeatures.filter(f => mask.has(f.name));
  return computeScoreFromFeatures(included);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to validate and handle invalid feature names?
- How would you scale gating across multiple model_versions?

## Why This Is Asked
This scenario tests real-time, multi-tenant cca_score with strict latency and verifiable provenance, requiring concrete API design, data modeling, and ledger trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time ingestion, per-tenant isolation, tamper-evident ledger (append-only log or Merkle root)
- Minimal data model with nonce and signature for replay protection
- Drift/poisoning detection, regional latency considerations
- Blockchain vs centralized ledger trade-offs (cost, latency, auditability)

## Code Example
```javascript
type ScoreEvent = {
  tenant_id: string;
  device_id_masked: string;
  timestamp: number;
  score_share: number;
  nonce: string;
  signature: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you prove ledger integrity to auditors without exposing raw data?
- How would you handle cross-region residency and regulatory constraints (GDPR/CCPA) in this design?
